.claude/*
# Track the reference skill installs: they are the framework's own dogfooding and
# the copy every adopter installs from, not maintainer-local state. Kept untracked,
# the canonical frontmatter-correct SKILL.md files were invisible to git and drifted
# from templates/ without anything noticing.
!.claude/skills/
# Anchored: this is the maintainer's own memory dir at the repo root, not every
# directory named memory/ anywhere. Unanchored it also swallowed
# templates/test-fixtures/memory/ — so any NEW fixture added there was silently
# unaddable and showed nothing in git status. The ten fixtures already tracked
# predate the rule and were unaffected, which is why it went unnoticed.
/memory/
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.stackdump
__pycache__/
